models: one output projection for all the ubatch's tokens in the Qwen gated delta net layers

Qwen3.5/3.6 (qwen35, qwen35moe), Qwen3-Next and qwen4exp shaped the input of a linear-attention
layer's output projection (ssm_out) as [value_dim, n_seq_tokens, n_seqs]. In a decode step every
sequence has one token, so the product had a single column and n_seqs batches: the CUDA/HIP backend
took the matrix-vector kernel once per sequence and read ssm_out's weights n_seqs times. Measured
with rocprof on one MI250X GCD (Qwen3.6-27B Q4_K_M, llama-batched-bench, 32 sequences answering):
that kernel took 0.71 ms a call against 0.05 ms with one sequence, 22% of the GPU time. As
[value_dim, n_tokens] it is one matrix product reading the weights once. Same arithmetic per
element, in the matrix-matrix kernels' order.

diff --git a/src/models/qwen35.cpp b/src/models/qwen35.cpp
index 350cea8..7cbc215 100644
--- a/src/models/qwen35.cpp
+++ b/src/models/qwen35.cpp
@@ -468,7 +468,11 @@ ggml_tensor * llama_model_qwen35::graph::build_layer_attn_linear(
     ggml_tensor * attn_out_norm = build_norm_gated(output, model.layers[il].ssm_norm, z_2d, il);
 
     // Final reshape: [head_dim, n_heads, n_tokens, n_seqs] -> [n_tokens, n_seqs, n_heads * head_dim]
-    ggml_tensor * final_output = ggml_reshape_3d(ctx0, attn_out_norm, head_v_dim * num_v_heads, n_seq_tokens, n_seqs);
+    // EuLLM: one matrix of all the ubatch's tokens, not one per sequence. Shaped
+    // [value_dim, n_seq_tokens, n_seqs], a decode step of n sequences (one token
+    // each) went through the matrix-vector kernel once per sequence, reading
+    // ssm_out's weights n times; as [value_dim, n_tokens] it is one product.
+    ggml_tensor * final_output = ggml_reshape_2d(ctx0, attn_out_norm, head_v_dim * num_v_heads, n_seq_tokens * n_seqs);
     cb(final_output, "final_output", il);
 
     // Output projection
